    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d452-a1">

                <pb facs="0835" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg821"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore, collector,
                        to Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the
                        Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House, Collector’s
                            Office</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Philadelphia</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >November</hi> 9, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose the report of
                    E. O. Goodrich, esq., <pb facs="0836" n="822" xml:id="pg822"/> surveyor of the
                    port, in regard to an examination of the ram Atlanta, seized by instructions, on
                    the 8th instant, from your Department.</p>
                <p>Mr. Oakes Smith, with the Haytian general, waited on me this morning, and
                    produced evidence as leads me to believe that the Atlanta has been legitimately
                    purchased for the Haytain government. These gentlemen will wait on you, in a day
                    or two, in regard to the vessel.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HENRY D. MOORE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector of
                        Customs.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. S. Boutwell</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
